    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="31">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Ine">Ine</ref> 31</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="31" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="102" ed="#liebermann"/>LXXV. Gif mon wíf gebycge<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#Ine_31.lnote.oe.12"/>, ⁊ sio gyft forð ne cume, agife<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Ine_31.lnote.oe.13-2"/> þæt feoh ⁊ forgielde<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Ine_31.lnote.oe.14-2"/> ⁊ gebete þam<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Ine_31.lnote.oe.15-2"/> byrgean, swa his borgbryce<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Ine_31.lnote.oe.16-2"/> sie.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="31" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="102" ed="#liebermann"/>LXXV. Gif mon<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_31.lnote.oe.2"/> wif bycge, ⁊ seo<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_31.lnote.oe.7"/> gift forð ne cume, agife ðæt feoh<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Ine_31.lnote.oe.8"/> ⁊ forgilde ⁊ gebete ðam byrgean, swa his borhbryce sy.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_31.lnote.oe.3"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="31" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="102" ed="#liebermann"/>Be þa<hi rend="italic">m</hi> þe man wif bycge, ⁊ seo gift wiðstande. Gyf mon wif bycge, ⁊ seo gyft forð ne cume, agyfe þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> feoh ⁊ forgylde ⁊ g<hi rend="italic">e</hi>béte ðam byrgean<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_31.lnote.oe.4"/>, swa his borhbryce sy.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="31" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="103" ed="#liebermann"/>Si quis emat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#Ine_31.lnote.oe.13"/> (sibi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#Ine_31.lnote.oe.14"/>) feminam et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#Ine_31.lnote.oe.15"/> donum (pretiumque) non<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#Ine_31.lnote.oe.16"/> compleatur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="17" target="#Ine_31.lnote.oe.17"/>, reddat ipsam pecuniam et persoluat et emendet plegio, sicut borghbreche<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#Ine_31.lnote.oe.18"/> sit (erit infractio plegii sui).</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="46" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be þam þe man wif bycge, ⁊ seo gift wiðstande.] Gif mon wíf gebyccge<ptr type="editorNote" n="7" target="#Ine_31.attnote.fn.7"/>, ⁊ sio gyft forð ne cume, agife þæt feoh ⁊ forgielde ⁊ gebete þam byrgean, swa his borgbryce sie.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="31" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="396" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{LXXV} Gif mon wíf gebyccge, ⁊ sio gyft forð ne cume, agife þæt feoh ⁊ forgielde ⁊ gebete þam byrgean swa his borgbryce sie.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Ine_31.lnote.de.1"/><pb n="103" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn man ein Weib [zur Ehe] kauft, die Braut-Übergabe [Trauung<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Ine_31.lnote.de.2"/>] jedoch<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Ine_31.lnote.de.3"/> nicht zu Stande kommt, gebe [der Braut-Vormund] das Geld<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Ine_31.lnote.de.4"/> [dem Bräutigam] zurück<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Ine_31.lnote.de.5"/> und bezahle [ihm] noch einmal<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Ine_31.lnote.de.6"/> so viel [zur Busse] und büsse dem [Verlobungs]bürgen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#Ine_31.lnote.de.7"/> so viel, wie der Bruch einer durch letzteren [geleisteten] Bürgschaft kostet.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#Ine_31.lnote.de.8"/></ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If someone buys a woman [in marriage], but the handing-over of the bride [the wedding] does not take place, let [the bride’s guardian] give the money back [to the bridegroom] and pay [him] as much again [as compensation], and compensate the [betrothal-]surety as much as the breach of a surety [given] by the latter costs.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="47" ed="#attenborough"/>If anyone buys a wife and the marriage does not take place, he [the bride's guardian] shall return the bridal price and pay [the bridegroom] as much again, and he shall compensate the trustee of the marriage according to the amount he is entitled to for infraction of his surety<ptr type="editorNote" n="1" target="#Ine_31.attnote.n.1"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="403" ed="#whitelock"/>If one buys a wife, and the marriage does not take place, the money is to be paid back, and as much again, and the surety is to receive compensation, as much as the breach of his surety<ptr type="editorNote" n="4" target="#Ine_31.whinote.n.4"/> cost.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="397" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If a man makes a contract for a wife, but the marriage does not take place, let [the bride’s guardian] return the bride-gift and compensate [the groom], and pay the guarantor [the price] for the breaking of his surety.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="397"><label>compare</label> <ref target="clause:Abt_77">Abt 77–81</ref> <quote>Compare Æthelberht §76 [L77–81].</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="397"><label>further insight into later practice</label> <ref target="clause:Wif_Inscr">Wif</ref> <quote>Wifmann's Beweddung provides further insight into later practice.</quote></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_31.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">borgan <hi rend="italic">im</hi> 16. <hi rend="italic">Jh. am Rande</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">borgan in the margin in the 16th cent.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_31.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">103</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">s. f. e. <hi rend="italic">Or</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">s. f. e. Or</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_31.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">103</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt K Co</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in K Co</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_31.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">103</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">nur</hi> et d. <hi rend="italic">Lond; nur</hi> pr. <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">only et d. Lond; only pr. the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_31.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">103</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">n. c. <hi rend="italic">doppelt K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">n. c. twice in K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_31.lnote.oe.17" n="17" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">103</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so Lond;</hi> -at <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus Lond; -at the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_31.lnote.oe.18" n="18" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">103</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">nur</hi> b. sit <hi rend="italic">Lond; nur</hi> e. i. p. s. <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">only b. sit Lond; only e. i. p. s. the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_31.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geänd. in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_31.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">eo <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">eo on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_31.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">e <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">e on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_31.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_31.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">gebycge, ⁊ seo <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">gebycge, ⁊ seo Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_31.lnote.oe.13-2" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">agyfe <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">agyfe Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_31.lnote.oe.14-2" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">forgyld <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">forgyld Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_31.lnote.oe.15-2" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ðæm <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ðæm Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Ine_31.lnote.oe.16-2" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">102</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">borhb. <hi rend="italic">ohne</hi> sie <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">borhb. without sie Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_31.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">73</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">B’s Rubrik braucht <hi rend="italic">wiðstandan</hi>, wofür Toller die Bed. ‘fern bleiben’ auch sonst nachweist</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">B’s rubric uses <hi rend="italic">wiðstandan</hi>, for which Toller attests the meaning ‘stay away’ elsewhere too</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_31.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">73</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘Brautkauf’ missversteht Q, der auch Wif 8 <hi rend="italic">giftan : dationi</hi> falsch übersetzt, als ob der Bräutigam zurücktrete, was bisherige Übersetzer übernehmen; ‘Morgengabe oder Wittum’ Price. Die Bed. ‘Heirat’ ist freilich meist nur für Plural belegt, kommt jedoch im Sing. bei Ostgermanen vor; so auch Toller s. v. II, Sweet <hi rend="italic">Reader</hi>. Und Ælfreds Gehilfe Wærferð braucht ihn für <hi rend="italic">nuptiae</hi> in Gregorii <hi rend="italic">Dial.</hi> ed. Hecht 199. <hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Eheschliessung 5g. h</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Q, who also mistranslates Wif 8 <hi rend="italic">giftan : dationi</hi>, misunderstands it as ‘bride-purchase’, as though the bridegroom were withdrawing; previous translators adopt this; ‘morning-gift or dower’ Price. The meaning ‘marriage’ is, it is true, mostly attested only for the plural, but it occurs in the singular among the East Germanic peoples; so also Toller s. v. II, Sweet <hi rend="italic">Reader</hi>. And Ælfred’s helper Wærferð uses it for <hi rend="italic">nuptiae</hi> in Gregorii <hi rend="italic">Dial.</hi> ed. Hecht 199. <hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Eheschliessung 5g. h</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_31.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">73</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">and</hi> ‘jedoch’ <hi rend="italic">s. Wb</hi> 4</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">and</hi> ‘however’: <hi rend="italic">see Wb</hi> 4</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_31.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">73</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Brautkauf. Younge (<hi rend="italic">Essays</hi> 170) und Sohm (<hi rend="italic">Trauung u. Verlob.</hi>) meinen: nur ein Angeld darauf, das Zeichen vollzogener Verlobung; allein die Doppelbusse der Westsachsen bedeutet sonst: <hi rend="spaced">ganze</hi> Schuld zweimal zahlen</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Bride-purchase. Younge (<hi rend="italic">Essays</hi> 170) and Sohm (<hi rend="italic">Trauung u. Verlob.</hi>) take it to be merely earnest money paid towards it, the sign of a completed betrothal; but elsewhere the double compensation of the West Saxons means paying the <hi rend="italic">whole</hi> debt twice</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_31.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">73</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Für <hi rend="italic">agiefan</hi> ‘zurückgeben’ <hi rend="italic">s. Wb</hi> und Toller <hi rend="italic">Suppl.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">For <hi rend="italic">agiefan</hi> ‘give back’ <hi rend="italic">see Wb</hi> and Toller <hi rend="italic">Suppl.</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_31.lnote.de.6" n="6" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">73</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. o.</hi> 9³</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">See above</hi> 9³</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_31.lnote.de.7" n="7" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">73</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Für den Bräutigam treten ebenfalls Bürgen auf; <hi rend="italic">s. Gl</hi> Eheschliessung 8r; Bürgschaft 7a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Sureties likewise appear on behalf of the bridegroom; <hi rend="italic">see Gl</hi> Eheschliessung 8r; Bürgschaft 7a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Ine_31.lnote.de.8" n="8" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">73</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">S. Gl</hi> Bürgschaftsbruch 1. 2</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">See Gl</hi> Bürgschaftsbruch 1. 2</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Ine_31.attnote.fn.7" n="7" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">46</biblScope></bibl><label>gebyccge</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">bycge</hi>. H &amp; B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="endnote" xml:id="Ine_31.attnote.n.1" n="1" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">186</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="en">This, substantially, is the rendering given by Thorpe and Liebermann. Price and Schmid, following the Latin version, understand <hi rend="italic">gyft</hi> as ‘bride-price,’ and interpret the law to mean that if the price to be paid by the bridegroom is not forthcoming, the bridegroom must not only pay this, but he must also make amends, etc.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="Ine_31.whinote.n.4" n="4" source="#whitelock"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">403</biblScope></bibl><label>surety</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">borgbryce;</hi> this term is often used to cover the same complex of rights as <hi rend="italic">mundbryce</hi>. On <hi rend="italic">mund, see</hi> p. 365.</seg></note>
      </div>
